{
  "about": "The Dataset-JSON source profiles read through the file route (DSJSON-1 to DSJSON-5, INPUT-1, INPUT-3, INPUT-9): a .json input is the single-object representation and an .ndjson input the newline-delimited one; each column's dataType types its field through the closed table, which a types entry may only narrow; members the profile does not read are skipped; and each closed cause, and a value that does not parse, reports its complete issue. Every input file was written by hand from the standard's schema, and every expected row and byte was derived by hand from the rule cards: CSV-5 writes each value read, a decimal's text reads as a number under VALUE-6, and a datetime without seconds is written with them (VALUE-15, VALUE-17).",
  "documents": {
    "spec": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: VS\nkeys: [USUBJID]\ninput: {SRC: input/vs.json}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [USUBJID, VISITNUM, VSSTRESN, VSORRES, WEIGHT, VSDT, VSDTM, VSTM, VSLINK]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: USUBJID, type: str, derivation: SRC.USUBJID}\n  - {name: VISITNUM, type: int, derivation: SRC.VISITNUM}\n  - {name: VSSTRESN, type: float, derivation: SRC.VSSTRESN}\n  - {name: VSORRES, type: float, derivation: SRC.VSORRES}\n  - {name: WEIGHT, type: float, derivation: SRC.WEIGHT}\n  - {name: VSDT, type: date, derivation: SRC.VSDT}\n  - {name: VSDTM, type: datetime, derivation: SRC.VSDTM}\n  - {name: VSTM, type: str, derivation: SRC.VSTM}\n  - {name: VSLINK, type: str, derivation: SRC.VSLINK}\n",
